let __v_1993 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"divided\",\"divide\",\"half in the sauce\",\"reserve\"]},\"\\\\bdivid(?:ed|e)\\\\b\",\"'Divided' means the amount is split between stages: half the cheese in the sauce and half on top, or the butter half in the cake and half in the icing. Weigh or measure the whole lot out and set the second part aside in a bowl before you start, or it is easy to tip it all in at once.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"until\",\"cue\",\"how do i know when it is done\"]},\"\\\\buntil\\\\b\",\"'Until' is a cue, not a time: until golden, until it comes away from the pan, until a skewer comes out clean. The recipe gives you the sign to look for because the clock cannot - ovens and tins differ - so trust your eyes and nose first and the timer second.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mise en place\",\"prep\",\"prepped\",\"prep ahead\"]},\"\\\\bmise en place\\\\b|\\\\bprep\\\\b\",\"Mise en place is everything weighed, chopped and set out in bowls before you turn the heat on - the French for 'in place'. It is the whole trick of the last five minutes of a recipe: most dishes go wrong there because the onion was not chopped yet. Read the ingredients as a shopping-and-chopping list and do all of it first.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cup\",\"cups\",\"what is a cup\"]},\"\\\\bcups?\\\\b\",\"A cup in a recipe is a volume: 240ml, or 8 US fluid ounces, which is a bit over half a pint. Most British recipes weigh in grams instead and a British teacup is not a US cup, so a recipe that says cups is written in American measures - and a cup of flour is about 120g, a cup of sugar about 200g.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"serves\",\"makes\",\"how many does it serve\"]},\"\\\\bserves\\\\b|\\\\bmakes\\\\b|\\\\bhow many\\\\b\",\"'Serves four' usually means four as a main with something alongside, and the number is a guide rather than a promise - a hungry four will finish a dish written for six. Halve or double the weights if your table is smaller or bigger, and keep the tin size and the time in mind when you do.\"]}]}")?;
