let __v_2320 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"football match\",\"before a match\",\"before the match\",\"playing sport\",\"five a side\",\"swimming gala\",\"cross country\",\"sports day\",\"before training\",\"game tomorrow\",\"before football\",\"before rugby\",\"before a run\",\"before swimming\",\"rugby match\",\"netball match\",\"hockey match\",\"match tomorrow\",\"before the game\",\"before his match\",\"before her match\",\"match on saturday\",\"match on sunday\",\"football tomorrow\",\"swimming gala\",\"sports day\"]},\"Feed them plain carbohydrate about three hours before, not straight before: a bowl of pasta with a little butter or cheese, a jacket potato, or toast and banana, plus water. Keep the fat and the fibre light so it is out of the stomach by kick-off, and have a banana or a flask of squash for after. A cold day wants a warm drink in a flask more than a bigger meal.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coeliac\",\"celiac\",\"gluten free\",\"gluten-free\",\"no gluten\",\"wheat allergy\"]},\"Cook one dish that is gluten-free by nature rather than making a second version: chicken thighs roasted with potatoes and lemon, a chilli with rice, or a fish pie with a mashed top. Check the stock cube, the soy sauce and the sausages, because that is where the wheat hides, use a clean board, and put the bread in its own basket so nothing is cross-contaminated.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"no oven\",\"oven is broken\",\"oven broke\",\"without an oven\",\"hob only\",\"just a hob\",\"oven is out\",\"no cooker\",\"microwave only\",\"moving house\"]},\"Everything on the hob: pasta with a sauce made in the same pan, rice with a stir fry, tinned tomatoes with beans and eggs poached in them, or soup with bread. One pan and one hob ring is plenty if you add the pasta to the sauce with a ladle of its water, and a kettle fills in for hot water.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tight budget\",\"on a budget\",\"skint\",\"no money\",\"cheap meals\",\"cheap dinners\",\"money is tight\",\"cutting back\",\"cost of living\"]},\"Build the week on eggs, lentils, beans, oats, frozen vegetables and chicken thighs: a lentil bolognese, a bean chilli, egg fried rice, a frittata and a soup covers five dinners for about the price of one takeaway. Frozen veg and tinned tomatoes cost less and waste less than fresh, and a whole chicken gives a roast plus a second meal from the carcass.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pregnant\",\"cant stand the smell\",\"can't stand the smell\",\"smell of cooking\",\"smells make me\",\"cooking makes me\"]},\"Eat cold or barely cooked while the smell turns your stomach: sandwiches, cereal, yoghurt, fruit, cheese and crackers, or a plate of the dinner you cooked yesterday eaten cold. Cook once in the morning when the kitchen is fresher, open a window and use the extractor, and let somebody else do the frying - it is the smell of hot fat that carries.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chest infection\",\"no appetite\",\"lost my appetite\",\"recovering from flu\",\"got the flu\",\"been ill\",\"feeling ill\",\"off my food\",\"cant eat\",\"can't eat\"]},\"Small and plain, eaten often: soup, toast, rice pudding, yoghurt, a banana, scrambled egg on a good day, and a drink beside you all day. Do not worry about a proper dinner while you are ill - calories and fluid are the job, and the appetite comes back with them.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"my back\",\"back is bad\",\"bad back\",\"cant stand long\",\"can't stand for long\",\"standing hurts\",\"on my feet all day\",\"knee is bad\",\"cant stand up\"]},\"One tray in the oven and one pot on the hob, done in about ten minutes of standing: chicken thighs or sausages with chopped veg and oil at 200C for 30 minutes, or a chilli you leave to simmer. Sit at the table to prep with everything within reach, use a stool at the hob, and cook double so tomorrow needs no standing at all.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"camping\",\"in a tent\",\"in the tent\",\"no fridge\",\"campervan\",\"camper van\",\"festival\",\"no electricity\"]},\"One pot, no fridge: pasta with tinned tomatoes, tinned beans and a chopped chorizo or a tin of tuna, or a curry from a jar with rice. Take food that keeps without cooling - tins, dried pasta, noodles, porridge oats, bread, hard cheese, apples - and a small gas ring plus matches in a plastic bag, because a wet night in a tent is when the cooking has to be simple.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"packed lunch\",\"packed lunches\",\"take to work\",\"take for lunch\",\"lunch for work\",\"lunchbox\",\"lunch box\",\"back at work\",\"back to work\",\"school lunch\",\"dinner lady\"]},\"Cook one extra portion of dinner and box it: rice, pasta or a grain with a protein and something sharp keeps a day in a cool bag and needs no microwave. If there is nothing left over, a flask of soup with bread, or a tub of couscous made with boiling water from a kettle and stirred with feta, tomato and herbs, takes five minutes the night before.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"night shift\",\"night shifts\",\"eats at 3am\",\"at 3am\",\"works nights\",\"working nights\",\"night worker\"]},\"Treat the shift as two meals: a proper one before you go in - rice, pasta or potato with protein and vegetables - then something light about two thirds of the way through, like a sandwich, yoghurt, fruit or cereal, rather than a full dinner at 3am. Heavy fat at that hour sits on the stomach and makes the last hours worse, and a flask of something warm helps more than coffee at the end of the shift.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pudding\",\"dessert\",\"to bring a cake\",\"bring a cake\",\"bring a dessert\",\"bbq\",\"barbecue\",\"pot luck\",\"bring something\"]},\"Bring something that travels and needs no fridge: a lemon drizzle traybake, brownies, a fruit crumble in its dish, or an Eton mess carried as meringue, cream and fruit in three tubs to layer at the table. Cut it in the tin so it arrives whole, and take the serving spoon with you.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tiny kitchen\",\"no worktop\",\"small kitchen\",\"no space\",\"little space\",\"one hob ring\",\"no surface\"]},\"One tray or one pan a night, prepped on a board balanced on the hob or the table: a traybake of chicken, potatoes and veg, a one-pot pasta where everything goes in together, or a stir fry chopped straight into the pan. Clear as you go so the board has a home, and cook double on the nights you have room, because the second meal needs no worktop at all.\"]}]}")?;
